      "Saints Akepsimas, Joseph and Aithalas": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar remembers Saints Akepsimas, Joseph and Aithalas, martyrs of Persia, on November 3. According to their traditional life, Akepsimas was bishop of the Christian community in the Persian city of Naesson, loved by his flock for his ascetic life and tireless pastoral work; Joseph was a priest and Aithalas a deacon. When the emperor Sapor ordered Christian clergy to be sought out and killed, the three were arrested, beaten and held in prison for three years. Brought before the emperor, they refused to worship the pagan gods and confessed their faith in Christ; the aged bishop was beheaded, and the priest and deacon were stoned.": 1,
      "Brief story based on the Orthodox Church in America. The date follows the Maronite calendar.": 3,
      "Read about Saints Akepsimas, Joseph and Aithalas": 1,
      "03.11.2026": 1,
