      "Saints Vitalis and Agricola": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar remembers Saints Vitalis and Agricola on November 4. The Catholic Encyclopedia relates that they were martyred at Bologna about 304 during Diocletian's persecution. Agricola, beloved for his gentleness, converted his servant Vitalis to Christianity, and the two became deeply attached to each other. Vitalis suffered martyrdom first; the persecutors then sought in vain, by tortures and by flattery, to win over Agricola, whom they finally crucified. Saint Ambrose's mention of the two martyrs in an oration is the only authority for their lives.": 1,
      "Brief story based on the Catholic Encyclopedia. The date follows the Maronite calendar.": 1,
      "Read about Saints Vitalis and Agricola": 1,
