      "Saint Paul, Patriarch of Constantinople": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar remembers Saint Paul, Patriarch of Constantinople, on November 6. According to his traditional life, Paul was chosen for the patriarchal throne of Constantinople after the death of Patriarch Alexander, when the Arian heresy had flared up again. He is remembered as a confessor who remained faithful to Christ during the Arian controversy.": 1,
      "Read about Saint Paul, Patriarch of Constantinople": 1,
