      "Saint Hieron and His Companions": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar remembers Saint Hieron and his companions, the thirty-three martyrs of Melitene, on November 7. According to their traditional life, Hieron was born in Tiana in Cappadocia and raised by a pious mother as a kindly and good Christian. Conscripted under emperors who persecuted Christians, he refused to serve them. At Melitene, Hieron and thirty-two other soldiers refused to offer sacrifice to the pagan gods and openly confessed their faith in Christ; after cruel tortures they were imprisoned and beheaded.": 1,
      "Read about Saint Hieron and his companions": 1,
